00:38:54,180 --> 00:38:57,370
在某一点，我们看到红色
At one specific point, we'll see red,

707
00:38:57,490 --> 00:39:00,740
或一只鸟，可能闪现橙色
or to a certain bird, it may fluoresce orange.

708
00:39:00,860 --> 00:39:02,210
或者某个动物
Or to some animals,

709
00:39:02,330 --> 00:39:07,050
他们可以看到雷达波或紫外线
they can actually see radar or ultraviolet.

710
00:39:07,160 --> 00:39:09,050
而这一切
So all of these things

711
00:39:09,170 --> 00:39:11,650
不是由外在世界决定的
are not determined by the external world.

712
00:39:11,770 --> 00:39:13,220
它们是由我们界定的
They're determined by us.

713
00:39:13,340 --> 00:39:14,490
所以是我们的大脑
So it's our mind

714
00:39:14,600 --> 00:39:17,830
产生了这些主观经验
that actually makes that subjective experience.

715
00:39:17,940 --> 00:39:19,660
所以“生物中心论”是唯一合理的途径
So biocentrism is the only rational way

716
00:39:19,780 --> 00:39:21,600
来解释宇宙的结构
to explain the structure of the Universe.

717
00:39:21,710 --> 00:39:25,300
罗伯特的激进理论源于对
Robert's radical theory stems from pondering

718
00:39:25,410 --> 00:39:28,510
另已被广泛接受一个奇怪的理论的沉思
another strange theory that is widely accepted --

719
00:39:28,620 --> 00:39:30,670
即量子力学
quantum mechanics.

720
00:39:30,790 --> 00:39:35,780
在量子理论中，粒子可以同时位于多重地点
In quantum theory, particles can be in multiple places at once.

721
00:39:35,890 --> 00:39:37,850
直到你做出观测
Until the moment you make a measurement,

722
00:39:37,960 --> 00:39:42,420
那时粒子必须终止于其中的某一个位置
when the particle must end up in only one of those locations.

723
00:39:42,530 --> 00:39:44,820
意味着在观测者
Which means nothing is certain

724
00:39:44,930 --> 00:39:48,570
观测之前，没有什么是确定的
until an observer makes a measurement.

725
00:39:53,170 --> 00:39:56,930
罗伯特认为我们必须将微观世界的规则
Robert thinks we must apply the rules of the microscopic world

726
00:39:57,050 --> 00:39:59,640
应用于日常经验中
to our everyday experiences.

727
00:39:59,750 --> 00:40:03,270
我们看、听、接触
Since everything we see, hear and touch

728
00:40:03,390 --> 00:40:06,010
都是由微观粒子组成
is made up of microscopic particles,

729
00:40:06,120 --> 00:40:09,380
这使他怀疑
which led him to wonder,

730
00:40:09,490 --> 00:40:13,550
当森林中一刻树倒下的时候 究竟发生了什么
what really happens when a tree falls in the woods?

731
00:40:13,660 --> 00:40:15,190
当林中的树倒下
So when a tree falls in the forest,

732
00:40:15,300 --> 00:40:16,990
它产生了空气压力扰动
it creates an air pressure disturbance.

733
00:40:17,100 --> 00:40:18,390
基于简单的科学
According to simple science,

734
00:40:18,500 --> 00:40:21,590
无论有没有人观测 这都会发生
that occurs whether or not anyone is there to observe it.

735
00:40:21,700 --> 00:40:24,230
但我们知道一个事实，没有观测者
But we know for a fact that without the observer,

736
00:40:24,340 --> 00:40:27,160
没有树或空气的一个粒子
that not a single particle in the tree or the air itself

737
00:40:27,280 --> 00:40:29,000
以确切的目的存在
exists with definite properties.

738
00:40:29,110 --> 00:40:32,940
除非有人观察到
So unless someone is actually observing the tree falling,

739
00:40:33,050 --> 00:40:36,140
树倒下时没有粒子产生噪声
there are no particles there to make the noise.

740
00:40:36,250 --> 00:40:39,080
当你没有注意到的时候，那里没有声音
So without your consciousness, there's no sound.

741
00:40:39,190 --> 00:40:41,340
同时，那里没有树
Indeed, there's no tree.

742
00:40:41,460 --> 00:40:44,710
我们周围的物理世界全是
The physical world around us is all an illusion,

743
00:40:44,830 --> 00:40:47,820
我们思维创造的幻象
created by our minds,

744
00:40:47,930 --> 00:40:50,350
当我们闭上眼睛
and when we close our eyes,

745
00:40:50,470 --> 00:40:54,820
空间和时间都消融了
space and time simply dissolve away.

746
00:40:54,940 --> 00:40:56,290
实际上是我们
Well, it's actually us, the observer,

747
00:40:56,410 --> 00:40:58,330
即观测者自己创造了时间空间，
这就是之所以你现在在那里
who creates space and time, and that's why you're here now.

748
00:40:58,440 --> 00:41:02,400
现实自始至终都关乎于观测者
Reality begins and ends with the observer.

749
00:41:02,510 --> 00:41:06,370
罗伯特·兰札的“生物中心论”激进地建立在
Robert Lanza's biocentrism is a radical spin

750
00:41:06,480 --> 00:41:10,210
量子力学无可否认的陌生之上
on the undeniable strangeness of quantum mechanics.

751
00:41:10,320 --> 00:41:13,110
量子计算专家赛斯·劳埃德
Quantum computation expert Seth Lloyd

752
00:41:13,220 --> 00:41:15,140
注意到生物和宇宙间
sees a different connection

753
00:41:15,260 --> 00:41:18,150
一种不同的联系
between biology and the Universe --

754
00:41:18,260 --> 00:41:21,890
一种争议更少，但同样令人兴奋的联系
one that is less controversial, but just as mind-blowing.

755
00:41:22,000 --> 00:41:24,420
他认为自大爆炸以来
He believes that every single thing

756
00:41:24,530 --> 00:41:27,020
发生的每个独立事件
that has happened since the Big Bang

757
00:41:27,140 --> 00:41:29,730
是宇宙仍在进行的
is part of a colossal computation

758
00:41:29,840 --> 00:41:32,460
巨大的量子计算的一部分
that the Universe is still making.

759
00:41:32,580 --> 00:41:38,230
在宇宙广阔的0和1的矩阵中
And within the universe's vast array of atomic 0s and 1s

760
00:41:38,350 --> 00:41:41,640
存在着可能是宇宙本身的最高成就——
exists what could be its crowning achievement --

761
00:41:41,750 --> 00:41:44,170
生物学生命
biological life.

762
00:41:44,290 --> 00:41:46,780
所以宇宙时常产生
So the Universe is constantly generating

763
00:41:46,890 --> 00:41:49,080
一些随机信息比特
little random bits of information.

764
00:41:49,190 --> 00:41:50,810
此刻，不时地
Now, every now and then,

765
00:41:50,930 --> 00:41:54,550
某一微小的随机波动会被捕获
one of these little random fluctuations will take hold

766
00:41:54,660 --> 00:41:56,950
并被放大到巨大尺度
and get amplified to a large scale

767
00:41:57,070 --> 00:42:00,960
开始产生宇宙中真正巨大的结果
and start to have really massive consequences in the Universe.

768
00:42:01,070 --> 00:42:04,930
可以认为 当生命出现并创造DNA之时
You could say that when life came along and created DNA,

769
00:42:05,040 --> 00:42:08,570
一个从不间断的计算早已在进行
that there was already an ongoing computation going on,

770
00:42:08,680 --> 00:42:13,270
这些生命研究出黑入这一不间断计算的方法
and life figured out how to hack into that ongoing computation

771
00:42:13,380 --> 00:42:18,950
成为当中的一部分，做出与众不同的新奇的什么事情
to make a piece of it do something novel and different.

772
00:42:21,060 --> 00:42:24,460
考虑宇宙是单一生命体
To think of the Universe as a single, living thing

773
00:42:25,100 --> 00:42:28,790
很考验我们的想象力
stretches our imaginations quite a bit.

774
00:42:28,910 --> 00:42:31,430
宇宙可能由心跳驱动
The cosmos could be driven by a heartbeat

775
00:42:31,540 --> 00:42:33,800
每万亿年
that pumps out clusters of galaxies

776
00:42:33,910 --> 00:42:36,700
泵出成簇的星系
once every trillion years.

777
00:42:36,810 --> 00:42:39,740
我们可能是其他宇宙的子孙
We could be the child of another universe

778
00:42:39,850 --> 00:42:42,010
并产生数不尽的后代
and be spawning countless more.

779
00:42:42,120 --> 00:42:45,940
或者宇宙是被一种
Or the cosmos could be a giant computation,

780
00:42:46,060 --> 00:42:51,980
叫做“生物学生命"的电脑病毒 感染的巨型计算
infected by a computer virus called biological life.

781
00:42:52,100 --> 00:42:55,790
我们无法确定谁更具生机
And we can't tell who is more alive --

782
00:42:55,900 --> 00:43:00,000
宇宙还是我们
The Universe or us.

